WEBVTT

00:00:11.715 --> 00:00:12.755
Sit down, Bob.

00:00:17.915 --> 00:00:22.435
I'm not happy, Bob.
Not happy.

00:00:23.035 --> 00:00:24.395
Ask me why.

00:00:24.475 --> 00:00:26.115
Okay. Why?

00:00:26.195 --> 00:00:27.955
Why what?
Be specific, Bob.

00:00:28.075 --> 00:00:29.675
Why are you unhappy?

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:31.595
Your customers
make me unhappy.

00:00:31.715 --> 00:00:33.395
What, you've
gotten complaints?

00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:34.955
Complaints I can handle.

00:00:35.075 --> 00:00:38.715
What I can't handle
is your customers'
inexplicable knowledge

00:00:38.795 --> 00:00:40.635
of Insuricare's
inner workings!

00:00:40.715 --> 00:00:42.715
They're experts.
Experts, Bob!

00:00:42.795 --> 00:00:45.795
Exploiting every loophole,
dodging every obstacle!

00:00:45.915 --> 00:00:48.435
They're penetrating
the bureaucracy!

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:50.155
Did I do
something illegal?

00:00:50.275 --> 00:00:51.275
No.

00:00:51.355 --> 00:00:53.355
We shouldn't help
our customers?

00:00:53.435 --> 00:00:55.635
The law requires
that I answer no.

00:00:55.715 --> 00:00:56.955
We're supposed
to help people.

00:00:57.075 --> 00:00:59.075
(YELLING)
Help our people!

00:00:59.155 --> 00:01:00.995
Starting with
our stockholders.

00:01:01.075 --> 00:01:03.475
Who's helping
them out, huh?

00:01:05.555 --> 00:01:09.915
You know, Bob,
a company...

00:01:09.995 --> 00:01:11.235
Is like
an enormous clock.

00:01:11.315 --> 00:01:15.275
...is like an enormous...
Yes. Precisely.

00:01:15.355 --> 00:01:20.675
It only works if all
the little cogs mesh
together.

00:01:20.755 --> 00:01:23.355
Now, a clock
needs to be cleaned,

00:01:23.435 --> 00:01:25.915
well-lubricated
and wound tight.

00:01:25.995 --> 00:01:28.235
The best clocks
have jewel movements,

00:01:28.315 --> 00:01:30.995
cogs that fit,
that cooperate
by design.

00:01:31.115 --> 00:01:33.275
(CHUCKLING) I'm being
metaphorical, Bob.

00:01:33.355 --> 00:01:35.835
Know what I mean
by cooperative cogs?

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:37.675
Bob?

00:01:37.755 --> 00:01:41.115
Bob? Look at me
when I'm talking
to you, Parr.

00:01:41.195 --> 00:01:42.595
That man out there,
he needs help.

00:01:42.675 --> 00:01:44.155
Don't change
the subject.

00:01:44.235 --> 00:01:45.755
We're discussing
your attitude.

00:01:45.835 --> 00:01:47.315
He is getting mugged!

00:01:47.395 --> 00:01:49.955
Well, let's hope
we don't cover him.
I'll be right back.

00:01:50.035 --> 00:01:53.555
Stop right now
or you're fired!

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:58.235
Close the door.

00:02:00.035 --> 00:02:02.355
Get over here, now.

00:02:06.035 --> 00:02:09.675
I'm not happy, Bob.
Not happy.

00:02:10.715 --> 00:02:12.515
He got away.

00:02:12.595 --> 00:02:14.355
Good thing, too.

00:02:14.435 --> 00:02:17.035
You were this close
to losing your...

00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:21.715
(MOANING)

00:02:26.315 --> 00:02:27.475
Uh-oh.

00:02:29.195 --> 00:02:32.835
(OVER PA) Please report
to operating room 722
immediately.

00:02:39.755 --> 00:02:40.995
How is he?
He'll live.

00:02:41.075 --> 00:02:42.915
I'm fired, aren't I?
You think?

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:43.995
What can I say, Rick?

00:02:44.075 --> 00:02:45.155
Nothing you haven't
said before.

00:02:45.235 --> 00:02:46.315
Someone was
in trouble.

00:02:46.395 --> 00:02:47.515
Always.

00:02:47.595 --> 00:02:49.155
I had to do something.

00:02:49.275 --> 00:02:50.475
Every time
you say that,

00:02:50.555 --> 00:02:52.755
it's a month and a half
of trouble for me.

00:02:52.835 --> 00:02:55.195
Hundreds of thousands
of taxpayer's dollars.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.275
I know.

00:02:56.355 --> 00:02:57.675
We pay to keep
the company quiet.

00:02:57.755 --> 00:03:00.835
We pay damages,
erase memories,
relocate your family.

00:03:00.915 --> 00:03:03.675
Every time it gets harder.
Money, money, money.

00:03:03.755 --> 00:03:07.755
We can't keep doing this.
We appreciate what you
did in the old days,

00:03:07.835 --> 00:03:09.115
but those days are over.

00:03:09.235 --> 00:03:11.195
From now on,
you're on your own.

00:03:14.395 --> 00:03:15.675
Listen, Bob.

00:03:15.755 --> 00:03:18.715
Maybe I could
relocate you, you know,
for old times' sake.

00:03:18.795 --> 00:03:20.675
I can't do that
to my family.

00:03:20.755 --> 00:03:22.115
Everyone just got settled.

00:03:22.195 --> 00:03:24.395
I'll make it work.
Thanks.

00:03:24.475 --> 00:03:26.515
Take care
of yourself.

00:03:38.795 --> 00:03:40.875
What are you
waiting for?

00:03:40.955 --> 00:03:44.955
I don't know.
Something amazing,
I guess.

00:03:45.635 --> 00:03:48.235
(SIGHS) Me, too, kid.

00:03:52.235 --> 00:03:53.315
(SIGHS)

00:03:54.555 --> 00:03:55.995
(DOOR SWINGS SHUT)

00:04:03.955 --> 00:04:05.435
(GROANS)

00:04:11.155 --> 00:04:12.155
Huh?

00:04:25.155 --> 00:04:26.515
"Hold still"?

00:04:26.595 --> 00:04:28.995
COMPUTER: Match,
Mr. Incredible.

00:04:35.195 --> 00:04:38.395
Room is secure.
Commence message.

00:04:38.475 --> 00:04:42.795
MIRAGE:
Hello, Mr. Incredible.
Yes, we know who you are.

00:04:42.875 --> 00:04:45.875
Rest assured,
your secret is
safe with us.

00:04:45.955 --> 00:04:49.435
My name is Mirage.
We have something
in common.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:53.195
According to the government,
neither of us exist.

00:04:53.275 --> 00:04:55.955
Please pay attention,
as this message
is classified

00:04:56.035 --> 00:04:57.795
and will not
be repeated.

00:04:57.875 --> 00:05:00.315
I represent
a top secret division
of the government,

00:05:00.395 --> 00:05:02.595
designing and testing
experimental technology,

00:05:02.675 --> 00:05:05.875
and we have need of
your unique abilities.

00:05:05.995 --> 00:05:08.235
Something happened
at our testing facility.

00:05:08.315 --> 00:05:09.795
HELEN: Honey!
Huh? What?

00:05:09.915 --> 00:05:11.635
Dinner's ready.
Okay.

00:05:11.715 --> 00:05:14.235
...it is contained
within an isolated area,

00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:18.635
it threatens to cause
incalculable damage to
itself and our facilities,

00:05:18.715 --> 00:05:21.475
jeopardizing hundreds
of millions of dollars...

00:05:21.555 --> 00:05:23.155
HELEN:
Is someone in there?

00:05:23.235 --> 00:05:24.835
It's the TV,
trying to watch.

00:05:24.915 --> 00:05:26.475
Because of its
sensitive nature...

00:05:26.595 --> 00:05:28.835
HELEN: Stop.
It's time for dinner.

00:05:28.915 --> 00:05:29.915
One minute!

00:05:30.395 --> 00:05:33.835
If you accept,
your payment will be triple
your current annual salary.

00:05:33.915 --> 00:05:35.355
Call the number
on the card.

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:37.835
Voice-matching
will ensure security.

00:05:37.915 --> 00:05:40.515
The supers aren't gone,
Mr. Incredible.

00:05:40.595 --> 00:05:41.755
You're still here.

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:45.795
You can still do
great things. Or

00:05:45.875 --> 00:05:49.075
you can listen to
police scanners.
Your choice.

00:05:49.275 --> 00:05:51.115
You have 24 hours
to respond.

00:05:51.195 --> 00:05:53.475
Think about it.

